I would also like to use such a function. However, it may not be possible for some models because whether a parameter is free or not may also depend on arguments used when calling sem() or cfa(). E.g.,

``` r
library(lavaan)
#> This is lavaan 0.6-16
#> lavaan is FREE software! Please report any bugs.
model <- '
visual  =~ x1 + x2 + x3
textual =~ x4 + x5 + x6
'

fit1 <- cfa(model, data = HolzingerSwineford1939)
parameterEstimates(fit1)[1:6, ]
#>       lhs op rhs   est    se      z pvalue ci.lower ci.upper
#> 1  visual =~  x1 1.000 0.000     NA     NA    1.000    1.000
#> 2  visual =~  x2 0.559 0.105  5.301      0    0.352    0.766
#> 3  visual =~  x3 0.708 0.118  6.004      0    0.477    0.939
#> 4 textual =~  x4 1.000 0.000     NA     NA    1.000    1.000
#> 5 textual =~  x5 1.111 0.065 16.996      0    0.983    1.239
#> 6 textual =~  x6 0.925 0.055 16.703      0    0.817    1.034

fit2 <- cfa(model, data = HolzingerSwineford1939, std.lv <http://std.lv> = TRUE)
parameterEstimates(fit2)[1:6, ]
#>       lhs op rhs   est    se      z pvalue ci.lower ci.upper
#> 1  visual =~  x1 0.907 0.087 10.376      0    0.735    1.078
#> 2  visual =~  x2 0.507 0.079  6.423      0    0.352    0.661
#> 3  visual =~  x3 0.642 0.078  8.270      0    0.490    0.794
#> 4 textual =~  x4 0.991 0.057 17.491      0    0.880    1.102
#> 5 textual =~  x5 1.101 0.063 17.545      0    0.978    1.223
#> 6 textual =~  x6 0.917 0.054 17.079      0    0.811    1.022
```

<sup>Created on 2023-09-28 with [reprex v2.0.2](https://reprex.tidyverse.org)</sup>

In the example above, the model syntax is the same. However, whether the loadings of x1 and x4 are free depends on the value of std.lv <http://std.lv>.

-- Shu Fai

