Ah. Okay. Basically, you have 3 options (maybe a few more, but these 3 come to mind):

(1) Create the syntax from the edited lavaanify object. I think Shu Fai posted something about this recently.
(2) Use the placeholders as suggested by Shu Fai and write a function that exchanges the placeholders for the labels. I posted something about this on stackoverflow some time ago (last post. gsub.rec function): https://stackoverflow.com/questions/29403080/match-and-replace-multiple-strings-in-a-vector-of-text-without-looping-in-r
(3) Write the original code in a more machine friendly way(probably some form of list) and write a function that creates the model syntaxes you want.

Best

Christian

